msgid "Pedigree Tour"
msgstr ""

#: src/user/applications/tour/main.cc:54
msgid "Here is the root filesystem:"
msgstr ""

#: src/user/applications/tour/main.cc:62
msgid ""
"Pedigree uses a conventional filesystem layout. Programs and libraries are "
"under /usr, configuration is under /etc, user homes are under /home, and "
"runtime state is under /run."
msgstr ""

#: src/user/applications/tour/main.cc:72
msgid ""
"Device files are available under /dev, process information under /proc, and "
"temporary files under /tmp."
msgstr ""

#: src/user/applications/tour/main.cc:81
msgid ""
"If something goes wrong, you may find yourself in the Pedigree kernel "
"debugger. This can also be accessed on-demand by pressing F12 at any time."
msgstr ""

#: src/user/applications/tour/main.cc:91
msgid ""
"In the debugger, you can read the kernel log, view backtraces, and do "
"various other inspections to identify what went wrong or inspect kernel "
"state."
msgstr ""

#: src/user/applications/tour/main.cc:102
msgid ""
"You can use the `help` command to see what is available in the debugger. If "
"you run into an issue that triggers the debugger, please try and add a "
"serial port log if you report it to us. Thanks!"
msgstr ""

#: src/user/applications/tour/main.cc:114
msgid ""
"The tour is now complete, and you are now better-equipped to handle "
"Pedigree! Raise any issues you find at https://github.com/miselin/pedigree/"
"issues.\n"
"\n"
"Thank you for trying out Pedigree!"
msgstr ""
